{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And the light of Israel.</b> It is HaShem, and the meaning concerns the angel who destroyed [n: Hebrew reads 'the angel who המכחיד the camp'; bracketed note in source indicates uncertainty whether to read הכחיד or המכחיד; rendered 'destroyed' as the translation of whichever reading.] the camp." "<b>His thorns and his briars.</b> The wicked."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The lemma reads 'the angel who המכחיד the camp'; the bracketed editorial note suggests reading הכחיד or the form as given, המכחיד; both mean 'destroyed/exterminated.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:12.639104071Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}